        <body>
            <div xml:id="d161">

                <pb facs="0177" n="105" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg105"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Lodge of the Friends of Perfect Union to Mrs.
                        Lincoln</hi>.</head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-volume-rules" calendar="gregorian"
                        notAfter="1865-07-31T23:59:59+00:09" notBefore="1865-04-15T00:00:00+00:09"
                        >undated</date>
                </dateline>
                <note rend="inline" rendition="#center" type="source">[Translation.]</note>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madam</hi>: Some misfortunes are irreparable, and
                    for which there is no consolation; these have fallen to your lot, and the world
                    deplores it.</p>
                <p>These are not then vain efforts of comfort we extend to you, but simply the
                    humble tribute of the profound regrets that weigh down our hearts. If the pure
                    and holy life of your great husband made him the favorite of a great nation, his
                    death has rendered him immortal.</p>
                <p>The liberator of slaves had to be a martyr! Was not the Nazarene crucified?</p>
                <p>Lincoln is now surrounded by a halo of glory that ages can never efface; his name
                    will be forever blessed.</p>
                <p>Be resigned, madam, to the inscrutable decrees of Providence, who needed a great
                    soul to accomplish its designs, and fixed upon the man most suited to its
                    purpose.</p>
                <p>We remain, madam, with the most profound respect, your very devoted servants.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>The officers of the lodge:</item>
                            <item>BOURGUET, <hi rendition="#italic">the Venerable</hi>.</item>
                            <item>D. RAYNAL, <hi rendition="#italic">1st Warden</hi>.</item>
                            <item>A. ROLLAND, 2<hi rendition="#italic">d Warden</hi>.</item>
                            <item>A. THERODEE, <hi rendition="#italic">Orator</hi>.</item>
                            <item>C. THOUBERT, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary</hi>.</item>
                            <item>J. MERIE, <hi rendition="#italic">Keeper of the Seals</hi>.</item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
